## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

1. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the 3637739 byte gap (per W44-66
   user correction).
2. DO NOT re-attempt the W44-29 entropy_mul lift wrapping on 3637739
   (W44-198 ruled out; not the lever).
3. DO NOT re-attempt the AC strategy selection mechanism on this
   cell (W44-199 ruled out; strategy at 98.4% parity).
4. DO NOT remove the cost-benefit gate in `compute_custom_orders`
   (`coeff_order.rs:411-503`) — W44-82 ruled out removal (+1595 B
   regression on 20 F-D + photo cells).
5. DO NOT tighten the cost-benefit gate WITHOUT a per-image
   discriminator — W44-200 dump confirms that 1418519 (WINNER)
   has bucket 3 DCT32x32 Y with end=0 (no DCT32x32 custom order
   computed at all for 1418519, only used_orders=0x1 = DCT8).
   The gate is doing the right thing on WINNERS; it's wrong on
   LOSERS in a content-dependent way.
6. DO NOT respawn this as a "find a single global fix" chunk. The
   measurement is conclusive that Zenjxl vs Libjxl modes produce
   different quant_ac on DCT32x32 Y for the same input, and no
   documented Section A-D gate explains it. Candidate A (per-block
   quant_ac VALUE dump) is the right next investigation.

